    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0677" n="1511" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/608</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-11T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 11, 2.41 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>265. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 988. I have received the following cable from Edwards: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>515, July 10, 4 p.m. For Sheldon from Edwards. Understand that within a
                            few days Dutch expect to put forth general proposal for supplying of
                            rations, granting of credit, etc. Garrett.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
